// Zenoh session for every one of robot_1's local ROS 2 nodes: system_main,
// its navigation capability node, robot_node, its own rviz2, and everything
// spawned for it by easynav_playground_kobuki's Kobuki simulation
// (robot_state_publisher, joint_state_publisher, the Gazebo bridge, ...).
// One shared file is safe here (unlike an earlier version of this config
// that needed a distinct fixed `id` per node): robot_1/zenoh_router.json5's
// ACL now recognizes "a local client" by *connecting over the Unix domain
// socket* (link_protocols), not by identity, so any number of processes can
// share this file -- validated directly that several concurrent unix-socket
// clients with no fixed id coexist without the collision a shared fixed id
// used to cause (see zenoh.md).
//
// mode: "peer" (not "client", despite these being pure local clients) --
// found empirically that "client" mode silently breaks delivery of
// TRANSIENT_LOCAL/latched publications (robot_description, /capabilities'
// JSON payload, ...) to a subscriber that joins after the one-shot publish;
// switching to "peer" (the same mode rmw_zenoh's own default session config
// uses) fixes it.
//
// Tried adding `gossip.autoconnect.peer: []` as defense in depth (so a
// local peer could never auto-connect straight to a gossip-discovered
// remote router, bypassing this robot's own router/ACL) -- empirically that
// setting *also* breaks the same TRANSIENT_LOCAL delivery this mode change
// was meant to fix, so it is intentionally left at its default here. The
// actual isolation guarantee doesn't depend on it anyway: it's enforced by
// robot_1/zenoh_router.json5's ACL on the boundary link itself (confirmed
// directly that a non-whitelisted topic still does not reach the central
// island with this exact session config). See zenoh.md for the full
// investigation, including why the ACL still holds regardless.
{
  mode: "peer",
  connect: { endpoints: ["unixsock-stream//tmp/easyfleet_robot_1_zenoh.sock"] },
  scouting: { multicast: { enabled: false } },
}
